b": "OCCURS_IN", "targetSlug": "grand-duchy-of-lithuania", "targetName": "Grand Duchy of Lithuania", "context": "Rumbaudas Valimantaitis held his primary administrative and military roles within the Grand Duchy of Lithuania."}, {"sourceSlug": "rumbaudas-valimantaitis", "sourceName": "Rumbaudas Valimantaitis", "verb": "INFLUENCES", "targetSlug": "grand-marshal-of-lithuania-office", "targetName": "Grand Marshal of Lithuania (office)", "context": "Rumbaudas Valimantaitis held the prestigious office of Grand Marshal of Lithuania for two decades (1412–1432), shaping its function during a pivotal era."}], "places": [{"name": "Samogitia, Grand Duchy of Lithuania", "role": "Elder's Province"}, {"name": "Vilnius, Grand Duchy of Lithuania", "role": "Administrative Center"}, {"name": "Toruń, Poland", "role": "Treaty Site"}], "texts": [{"title": "Wikipedia: Rumbaudas Valimantaitis", "type": "Reference article", "slug": "rumbaudas-valimantaitis"}], "externalLinks": ["https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q3920683", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rumbaudas_Valimantaitis"], "tags": ["Political Leaders", "political-systems", "geopolitical-linkage", "cause-and-effect"], "thumbnailUrl": "", "quote": "", "legacySummary": "", "historicalSignificance": {"significanceScore": 7, "significanceNarrative": "Rumbaudas Valimantaitis's long service as Elder of Samogitia and Grand Marshal was crucial in stabilizing the Grand Duchy of Lithuania's western frontiers against the Teutonic Order and consolidating central authority during a pivotal era, contributing to the rise of the Kęsgaila dynasty.", "significanceCategory": "regional"}, "_editLog": [{"timestamp": "2026-09-28T23:27:47Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#36496894012", "field": "summary", "oldValue": "Rumbaudas Valimantaitis was an influential Lithuanian noble of Zadora coat of arms. He was a son of Valimantas and brother of Mykolas Kęsgaila. He became Elder of Samogitia (1409–1411) and Grand Marshal (1412–1432).", "newValue": "Rumbaudas Valimantaitis (died 1433) was a formidable Lithuanian noble of the Zadora coat of arms, whose career as Elder of Samogitia (1409–1411) and Grand Marshal of Lithuania (1412–1432) placed him at the heart of the Grand Duchy's administration and its protracted conflicts with the Teutonic Order. The son of Valimantas and brother of Mykolas Kęsgaila, Rumbaudas represented a burgeoning native Lithuanian elite that gained significant influence under Grand Duke Vytautas the Great, helping to solidify the state's internal structure and external security during a period of intense geopolitical flux in Eastern Europe.

His tenure as Elder of Samogitia was particularly critical, coinciding with the Samogitian Uprising of 1409, which directly precipitated the Polish–Lithuanian–Teutonic War. After the decisive Battle of Grunwald in 1410, Rumbaudas played a role in the subsequent negotiations, culminating in the First Peace of Toruń (1411), which temporarily returned Samogitia to Lithuania. His subsequent appointment as Grand Marshal of Lithuania in 1412, a position he held for two decades, underscored his trusted status and administrative prowess, making him a central figure in the Grand Ducal court and its governance.

Rumbaudas Valimantaitis's legacy is intrinsically linked to the consolidation of the Grand Duchy of Lithuania's power and its territorial integrity in the early 15th century. His long and stable service in high offices provided continuity amidst shifting alliances and border disputes, contributing significantly to the administrative modernization initiated by Vytautas. The enduring political prominence of his family, particularly through his brother Mykolas Kęsgaila and his descendants, established a powerful aristocratic dynasty that would shape Lithuanian politics for generations, illustrating the deep roots of noble power in the Grand Duchy."}, {"timestamp": "2026-09-28T23:27:47Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#36496894012", "field": "detailsJson.causes", "oldValue": [{"title": "Medieval era: interplay of religious authority, feudal governance, and trade network expansion", "type": "EventWindow", "year": "1371, Grand Duchy of Lithuania"}, {"title": "Political crises and power transitions requiring new leadership", "type": "Idea", "year": "1371, Grand Duchy of Lithuania"}], "newValue": ["The ongoing strategic conflict between the Grand Duchy of Lithuania and the Teutonic Order necessitated strong regional leadership.", "The rising political influence of powerful Lithuanian noble families, such as the Valimantaitis clan, provided a pool of experienced administrators.", "Grand Duke Vytautas the Great's policy of centralizing power and appointing loyal nobles to key administrative posts created opportunities for figures like Rumbaudas."]}, {"timestamp": "2026-09-28T23:27:47Z", "editorId": "gemini-2.5-flash·cloud·GH#36496894012", "field": "detailsJson.effects", "oldValue": [{"title": "Shaped political institutions and governance practices", "type": "Idea", "year": "1433"}, {"title": "Contributed to synthesis of classical and religious thought informing Renaissance and Reformati", "type": "Movement", "year": "1433"}], "newValue": ["Rumbaudas's leadership helpe